{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# S8 — `rebar bridge suggest-mapping`: live Jira probe to pre-populate mapping config\n\n## Context / Problem\nEpic 3d7a (S1–S5) adds the config-driven mapping seam: a reserved `[mapping]` /\n`[tool.rebar.mapping]` block with per-layer vocabulary (`statuses`, `issue_types`,\n`link_types`, `hierarchy`) and axis maps (`status_map`, `type_map`, `link_map`,\n`priority_map`, `create_defaults`), parsed by\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/mapping_config.py` (S1). Authoring that block by\nhand is transcription-error-prone. S8 adds a READ-ONLY command that observes a live\nJira project through the pycontribs client and emits a suggested `[tool.rebar.mapping]`\nblock seeded with the project's real vocabulary and identity-seed axis maps.\n\nBlocking findings resolved:\n- Verb `rebar bridge probe` COLLIDES with the retired alias `bridge-probe`\n  (`_registry.py:579`; parser `_parsers/advanced/bridge.py:117`; handler `_bridge_probe`\n  at `_cli/__init__.py:103`, which CREATES+DELETES a throwaway issue — not read-only).\n  New verb: **`rebar bridge suggest-mapping`** (verified free in `src/`+`tests/`).\n- The probe must NOT use any private `_get_json` — that exists ONLY on the Gerrit client\n  (`review_bot/gerrit_client.py:128`), not the jira adapter, which uses only HIGH-LEVEL\n  `jira.JIRA` methods. The probe is grounded exclusively in such methods (below).\n- No tomlkit; TOML read via stdlib `tomllib`. `_emit_toml` is fail-closed on nesting, so\n  a DEDICATED nested emitter is added (below).\n\n## Approach\nNew verb wired into the bridge group (all NEW):\n- Parser: `commands.add_parser(\"suggest-mapping\", ...)` in\n  `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/bridge.py` (beside `check-access`, ~line 117),\n  taking `<PROJECT>` and `--write`.\n- Dispatch: add `\"suggest-mapping\"` to the pass-through set in `bridge_cli`\n  (`src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py:259`) plus a `_passthrough`/`_passthrough_help`\n  branch → NEW handler `_bridge_suggest_mapping` (`_cli/__init__.py`, sibling of\n  `_bridge_probe`).\n\nProbe (NEW `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/mapping_probe.py`, <800 LOC): a probe\nPORT with one narrow method per axis, each a thin call to a pycontribs `jira.JIRA`\nmethod. Default port built from `build_client_from_settings`\n(`adapters/jira_datacenter/transport.py:155`); tests inject a FAKE port with canned\nreturns → offline. Pin `jira>=3.8,<4` (pyproject.toml:202).\n\nAxis grounding — every axis uses a HIGH-LEVEL method (no private REST call):\n- `issue_types` vocab + `hierarchy` → `jira.JIRA.issue_types()` (documented public; read\n  each IssueType's `hierarchyLevel`). If `hierarchyLevel` is absent, the `hierarchy` axis\n  is DROPPED (emitted empty + note), not fabricated.\n- `priority_map` vocab → `jira.JIRA.priorities()` (documented public).\n- `link_types` vocab → `jira.JIRA.issue_link_types()` (documented public).\n- `statuses` vocab → `jira.JIRA.statuses()` (documented public). pycontribs exposes no\n  per-PROJECT status list publicly, so this is the GLOBAL set; the emitted block\n  documents that honest limitation.\n- `create_defaults` stubs → `jira.JIRA.createmeta_issuetypes(<KEY>)` +\n  `createmeta_fieldtypes(<KEY>, <issuetypeId>)` (documented public createmeta API); stub\n  only for a `required: true` field NOT in the outbound create BASELINE (see AC).\n- transition hints (best-effort) → grounded in the ACTUAL transitions surface:\n  `jira.JIRA.search_issues(jql)` (CONFIRMED in DC adapter) fetches one sample issue per\n  discovered type, then `jira.JIRA.transitions(issue)` (CONFIRMED at\n  `adapters/jira_datacenter/transitions.py:80`). Jira returns transitions only from each\n  sample's CURRENT status, so the set is inherently partial → flagged best-effort.\n  `status_map` stays identity-seeded; transition data is an ADVISORY marker, not complete.\n\nAnchor: `search_issues`, `transitions`, `fields` are confirmed in-repo on this same\n`jira.JIRA` client (DC adapter); the vocabulary getters are documented pycontribs 3.x\npublic API for that client.\n\nEmit: build `{\"projects\": {<KEY>: {<layer>}}}`.\n- Default (no `--write`): serialize that block to stdout as TOML. NEVER writes, issues\n  only reads.\n- `--write`: mirror `write_jira_config`'s read-whole/mutate/re-emit/atomic-replace\n  pattern. Target via `config._discover_project_config` → existing `rebar.toml`, else\n  create `<repo_root>/rebar.toml`; a user `pyproject.toml` is NEVER edited. Read with\n  `tomllib`, DEEP-MERGE under `[mapping.projects.<KEY>]` with EXISTING keys winning\n  (hand edits never clobbered), re-emit whole, atomic `os.replace`.\n\nSerialization (concrete): the `[mapping]` block needs NESTED tables\n(`[mapping.projects.KEY.status_map]`), but `_config_writer._emit_toml` is DELIBERATELY\nfail-closed on nested sub-tables — pinned by `tests/unit/test_jira_onboard.py:149`\n(`_emit_toml({\"jira\": {\"nested\": {\"k\": \"v\"}}})` must raise `ConfigError`). That guard is\nNOT touched. S8 adds a DEDICATED nested emitter `_emit_nested_toml` (new small helper in\n`_config_writer.py` or `mapping_probe.py`) that recurses into dict tables and writes\ndotted headers, used ONLY for `[mapping.*]`; `_emit_toml` and its pinned test are left\nas-is. `--write` deep-merges the parsed dict (stdlib `tomllib`), re-emits via the\ndedicated emitter + atomic `os.replace`, reusing `write_jira_config`'s target-selection\nand read-whole/mutate/re-emit shape. HONEST SCOPE: `tomllib` drops comments and there is\nno tomlkit, so the merge preserves existing hand-edited VALUES (existing keys win) but\ninline comments/formatting in `[mapping]` are NOT preserved on `--write` — documented in\nhelp, matching `_emit_toml`'s contract.\n\n## Scope\n- NEW `mapping_probe.py` (probe port + per-axis getters + layer builder + TOML emit),\n  <800 LOC.\n- NEW dedicated nested-table emitter `_emit_nested_toml` for `[mapping.*]` (in\n  `_config_writer.py` or `mapping_probe.py`); `_emit_toml`'s fail-closed-on-nested\n  contract and its pinned `tests/unit/test_jira_onboard.py:149` stay UNTOUCHED.\n- Wire the verb: `bridge.py` parser, `_bridge_commands.py` dispatch, `__init__.py`\n  handler (NEW).\n- Out of scope: WRITE to Jira; live-credential CI gating; comment round-tripping.\n\n## Testing\nAutomated tests use a FAKE probe port returning canned issue-type / priority / link-type\n/ status / createmeta / search+transitions data — fully offline, no live Jira or CI\ncredential (portability rule). A live smoke run is manual only, never a CI gate. New\ntests in `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_probe.py`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `test_probe_emits_mapping` — `rebar bridge suggest-mapping <KEY>` against the fake\n      port emits a `[tool.rebar.mapping]` block with discovered vocabulary\n      (`issue_types` via `issue_types()`, `statuses` via `statuses()`, `link_types` via\n      `issue_link_types()`, priorities via `priorities()`, `hierarchy` when\n      `hierarchyLevel` is present), identity-seed axis maps, and `create_defaults` stubs.\n- [ ] `test_probe_is_read_only` — default invocation writes NO file and the fake port\n      records only read calls (no create/transition/delete), distinct from\n      `check-access`.\n- [ ] `test_probe_write_preserves_edits` — `--write` deep-merges under `projects.<KEY>`;\n      a pre-existing hand-edited key in the target `rebar.toml` keeps its value (existing\n      keys win); `pyproject.toml` is never edited.\n- [ ] `test_probe_transitions_best_effort` — with the fake port returning `search_issues`\n      samples and per-issue `transitions()` limited to each sample's current status, the\n      emitted transition hints are flagged best-effort/partial (comment/marker), never\n      asserted complete; `status_map` remains identity-seeded.\n\n\"create_defaults\" baseline (concrete): the outbound create path\n`adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py:140-158` (`map_local_to_remote`) already supplies\n`summary`, `description`, `issuetype`, `priority`, `assignee`, and conditionally `status`\nand `parent`; a stub is emitted ONLY for a createmeta `required: true` field whose\nid/name is NOT in that baseline.\n\nTest tier: unit"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787356119691029001,"uuid":"9929d2f9-e979-4ef2-b917-3a36b633a791"}